=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: moving the pytest steps into a reusable workflow is a refactor, not a disabled step
origin: issue #181 bound — a step that leaves one workflow file produces no dead runner site, so
origin2: removal is not judged for workflows; the called workflow is new in the same diff.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    uses: ./.github/workflows/tests.yml
=== after: .github/workflows/tests.yml ===
name: tests
on:
  workflow_call:
jobs:
  pytest:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn", "path": ".github/workflows/ci.yml"}, {"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn", "path": ".github/workflows/tests.yml"}]
